    {
      "id": "l5",
      "companyId": "deepmind",
      "name": "Logan Kilpatrick",
      "handle": "@OfficialLoganK",
      "time": "4d",
      "text": "Today we are rolling out Gemini 4 Argon globally in the Gemini API, to Pro + Ultra in Gemini App, and Ultra subs in Antigravity! Argon is a huge step forward for Gemini, and a labor of love. This model has been battle tested by over 100,000 people at Google over the last month, with so much new innovation, ambition, and hard work baked into this release. The team has been heads down over the last 6 months working to make this possible across the stack (research, infra, safety, eng, etc). We rolled the model out to cyber defenders as part of our fairwind program and early access customers over the last 2 weeks, it has been amazing to see and talk to folks who are now using this model daily. Seeing the models writing capability, raw knowledge and persistence for coding, paired with new features like 1M token output when the model needs to work more has gotten me even more excited about our path ahead. This is just the start of the Gemini 4 era. As you saw with 3.5, 3.6, 3.7, and 3.8 Flash, our iteration speed with Gemini is fast : ) Now with Gemini 4 Argon to work from, I am cannot wait to see the progress continue, and most importantly see what this new model enables for the world. This is such a special moment in the arc of technology, as millions of people everyday tackle problems they could never have thought possible before. Gemini 4 Argon was built to help you tackle the hardest problems. I have personally felt this spark with Argon and hope you do too. Onwards!!",
      "replies": "1.2K",
      "reposts": "770",
      "likes": "11K",
      "inlineHandle": false,
      "url": "https://x.com/OfficialLoganK/status/2110038940841545827"
    },
    {
      "id": "l6",
      "companyId": "openai",
      "name": "Greg Brockman",
      "handle": "@gdb",
      "time": "3d",
      "text": "6 days and $40,000 of compute with GPT-5.6 Sol to find a critical vulnerability in Chrome, claiming Google’s first full-chain reward in 2026 for a vulnerability that would affect an estimated 1 billion users. Highlights the opportunity for defenders to utilize these tools to secure their software to unprecedented levels:",
      "replies": "262",
      "reposts": "329",
      "likes": "6.4K",
      "inlineHandle": false,
      "url": "https://x.com/gdb/status/2110063893016096831"
    },
    {
      "id": "l7",
      "companyId": "deepmind",
      "name": "Demis Hassabis",
      "handle": "@demishassabis",
      "time": "4d",
      "text": "Gemini 4 Argon is amazing for knowledge work and coding - and it’s super fun to build with! We asked it to create this wizard chess game and it's so cool to see Argon's physics understanding & 3D modelling capabilities, makes me nostalgic for Battlechess on the Amiga - fun times! Argon is rolling out today to Google Ultra and Pro subscribers in the @GeminiApp and Search, and Ultra subscribers in @antigravity! More info & full availability in the blog: https://t.co/7d3791mRNH",
      "replies": "360",
      "reposts": "518",
      "likes": "5.1K",
      "inlineHandle": false,
      "url": "https://x.com/demishassabis/status/2110041008100843835"
    },
